258
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,720
The salesperson told me

259
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,079
only two pieces were left

260
00:06:15,079 --> 00:06:15,760
and let me pick one

261
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,839
because each ring is different.

262
00:06:17,279 --> 00:06:18,720
Then, after I picked one

263
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,760
and bought it,

264
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:20,480
I really hoped

265
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,440
someone else

266
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,760
would grab the other ring soon,

267
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,679
so he couldn't get a chance to buy it.

268
00:06:24,679 --> 00:06:25,440
I even asked

269
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,239
the salesperson

270
00:06:26,239 --> 00:06:27,760
if they would restock it,

271
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:29,720
and they said restocks were unlikely.

272
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,000
So I planned that

273
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,880
when we met next time,

274
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:33,600
I'd give this ring to him

275
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,799
as a birthday surprise.

276
00:06:34,799 --> 00:06:35,519
After I handed it to him,

277
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,880
he opened the gift and said,

278
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,079
"Look, what is this?"

279
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,799
The second ring was bought by him.

280
00:06:44,799 --> 00:06:46,200
So at that time, I just thought...

281
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:47,760
Alright.

282
00:06:49,079 --> 00:06:50,519
That's perfect. Couple rings for you.

283
00:06:50,519 --> 00:06:52,760
Yeah, so now it has become...

284
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,519
Exactly.

285
00:06:53,519 --> 00:06:54,440
It became couple rings.

286
00:06:55,799 --> 00:06:56,519
